{"rules":[{"jurisdiction":"MA","level":"state","category":"security_deposits","status":"in_force","title":"Massachusetts security deposit limits, handling, interest and return (M.G.L. c. 186, § 15B)","requirement":"A security deposit may not exceed the first month's rent. It must be held in a separate interest-bearing Massachusetts bank account, and the tenant must get a receipt within 30 days naming the bank, location, amount and account number. The tenant must get a signed receipt when the deposit is received, and a written statement of the premises' condition within 10 days after tenancy commences or on receipt of the deposit, whichever is later. If the lessor holds the deposit for a year or longer, it must pay interest at 5% per year (or the lesser amount actually received from the bank) at the end of each year of the tenancy. The lessor must return the deposit, less permitted deductions, within 30 days after the tenancy ends. Permitted deductions are unpaid rent or water charges, unpaid tax increases under a conforming escalation clause, and reasonable repair of damage beyond normal wear and tear. Damage deductions require a sworn itemized list with cost evidence within the same 30 days. The lessor must keep deposit records for 2 years after the tenancy ends. The deposit and accrued interest must be transferred to a successor in interest. As amended effective Aug 1, 2025, the Executive Office of Housing and Livable Communities may by regulation authorize an optional fee in lieu of a security deposit, capped at 1 month's rent in total with any deposit.","key_value":"Max deposit = 1 month's rent; return within 30 days; interest 5%/yr (or lesser bank rate) after 1 year","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental tenancies in Massachusetts (leases and tenancies-at-will).","exemptions":"Does not apply to any lease, rental, occupancy or tenancy of 100 days or less that is for a vacation or recreational purpose.","coverage_logic":{"covers":null,"exempt":null},"subject":"landlord","interaction":"Any lease provision conflicting with this section, and any tenant waiver, is void and unenforceable as against public policy.","yields_to_local":false,"preempts_local":false,"effective_date":null,"effective_rule":null,"enacted_date":null,"end_date":null,"penalty":"Lessor forfeits the right to retain any part of the deposit for failure to comply with the account, itemized-list, successor-transfer or timely-return requirements. The tenant is awarded three times the deposit (or balance) plus 5% interest from the due date, court costs and reasonable attorney's fees. Failure to pay interest within 30 days after termination yields treble the interest owed plus costs and fees.","citation":"M.G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"a security deposit equal to the first month's rent provided that such security deposit is deposited as required by subsection (3) and that the tenant is given the statement of condition as required by subsection (2);","supporting_spans":["The lessor shall, within thirty days after the termination of occupancy under a tenancy-at-will or the end of the tenancy as specified in a valid written lease agreement, return to the tenant the security deposit or any balance thereof;","A lessor of residential real property who holds a security deposit pursuant to this section for a period of one year or longer from the commencement of the term of the tenancy shall, beginning with the first day of the tenancy, pay interest at the rate of five per cent per year, or other such lesser amount of interest as has been received from the bank where the deposit has been held payable to the tenant at the end of each year of the tenancy."],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_note":null},{"jurisdiction":"MA","level":"state","category":"application_screening_fees","status":"in_force","title":"Massachusetts cap on upfront payments at or before tenancy commencement (M.G.L. c. 186, § 15B(1)(b))","requirement":"At or before the start of a tenancy, a lessor (and, 